## MANUAL -- walked per the dispatch, both themes

**Contrast of the new instruction text, both themes.** Computed via
proper alpha-compositing of the full ancestor background chain (the dark
card background is semi-transparent `rgba(68,64,60,0.5)` over a
`rgb(41,37,36)` panel -- compositing required, a naive "first non-
transparent ancestor" read gives a false failing number; verified against
axe's own 0-violation finding on this element as ground truth, and visually
via a cropped screenshot):
  LIGHT: fg rgb(87,83,78) on bg rgb(250,250,249) -- ratio 7.30:1. PASS.
  DARK: fg rgb(168,162,158) on composited bg rgb(54.5,50.5,48) -- ratio
  4.99:1. PASS (≥4.5:1, point 7).
Screenshot: instr_dark.png -- legible amber-gray text, clearly visible.

**Hidden-disabled fields not focusable/announced while hidden.** Before
tick: #glide-path-fields has class `hidden`; the three inputs are
`disabled=true`, `required=false`; `glide-start-stock-pct.offsetParent`
is null (not merely visually hidden -- genuinely unreachable/non-
rendered). Tab from the checkbox skips over the entire glide-fields
region and lands on the next unrelated focusable control
(#inflation-rate-slider) -- confirmed same result light and dark.
Playwright `ariaSnapshot()` of `#glide-path-fields` while hidden is
EMPTY (no nodes at all in the accessibility tree -- strongest evidence:
not just excluded from tab order, excluded from the AT tree entirely).
After tick: ariaSnapshot shows the paragraph text, three correctly-
labelled spinbuttons ("Start %"/"End %"/"Years"), and the "Apply Glide
Path" button -- properly exposed. PASS, point 9/16.

**Tick/untick by keyboard.** Space on the focused checkbox (both
themes): ticking sets `checked=true`, removes `hidden` from
#glide-path-fields, flips the three inputs to `disabled=false,
required=true`, and fires NO network request (D6's contract). Unticking
(Space again) restores `hidden`, `disabled=true, required=false`, and
DOES submit (confirmed: unticking with blank/disabled fields still saves
enabled=false, matching the diff's documented design -- a disabled
control is excluded from constraint validation AND submitted form data).
Tab order after reveal: checkbox -> Start % -> End % -> Years, each with
its own `<label for>`, in visual order. PASS.

**Apply with an empty field -> browser validity, focus on field.**
Ticked (fields revealed, blank), clicked "Apply Glide Path": no
`/whatif/glide-path` request fires (native constraint validation stops
it before submission); `document.activeElement` is
`#glide-start-stock-pct` with `validationMessage: "Please fill out this
field."`, `validity.valid: false`. Confirmed identical in both themes.
Satisfies point 5's "focus moves to the first error on failed submit"
branch via native HTML5 validity (same mechanism already accepted for
the birth-month field in attempt 1). PASS.
Consequence noted: because Start %/End %/Years are now `required`
client-side, the server's own 400 message ("Start %, End %, and Years
are all required to apply a glide path") is not reachable through normal
keyboard/mouse UI -- it is a defense-in-depth backstop for a raw POST.
No a11y concern (nothing to announce that a real user can trigger).

**Refusal (D7) -- announced once, next to form, focus restored.**
Keyboard-activated (Enter) Christine's Remove button (linked to a
healthcare entry): optimistic removal (rows 2->1), debounced save
(~500ms) comes back refused, row restored (rows back to 2, both persons'
data intact), exactly 1 `[role=alert]` node reading "Remove Christine's
healthcare entry first" as the FIRST CHILD of the settings `<form>`
(next to the form), and focus returns to Christine's own restored Remove
button (`activeElement` is the BUTTON with text "Remove", not lost to
`<body>`). Repeating the identical failing action leaves alert count at
1 (pre-existing base.js/renderError short-circuit, unchanged by this
diff -- same behavior attempt 1 documented). PASS, matches dispatch ask
exactly.

